/*Q3.
Write a Java program that prompts the user to enter a letter of the alphabet and displays the succeeding letter in the alphabet series.

Input Format:
  - The input is a single letter from the alphabet series.

Output Format:
  - The output is the succeeding letter to the user-given letter.

Note:
  - The input character must be between letters A and Y (including) or a and y (including).
  - A partial code is provided in the editor.*/
/////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
/*Logic: Letters are consecutive in ASCII/Unicode. Input is guaranteed A to Y or a to y, so there is no wrap-around.*/

import java.util.Scanner;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        char ch = sc.next().charAt(0);
        char next = (char) (ch + 1);   // char arithmetic yields int, so cast back
        System.out.println(next);
        sc.close();
    }
}
